}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}$ and ${\\mathbf{a}}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.$ Find a basis $B$ of $\\text{span}\\{{\\mathbf{a}}_{1},{\\mathbf{a}}_{2},{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}\\}.$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find a subset of linearly independent vectors. So, we start by creating a matrix whose columns are made up of our vectors, and then we reduce the matrix to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, our matrix is already in a row echelon form.\n\nThe pivot columns correspond to linearly independent vectors, while the non-pivot columns correspond to linearly dependent vectors that can be removed. Here, the $1$st and $3$rd columns are pivot columns, while the $2$nd column is a non-pivot column.\n\nThe $1$st and $3$rd columns from the original matrix are ${\\mathbf{a}}_{1}$ and ${\\mathbf{a}}_{3}.$ So, a basis of $S$ is $\\{{\\mathbf{a}}_{1},{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}\\},$ that is to say, \n\n$$\nB=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345008 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7ab4781e-438b-5348-99ff-eec3eb4e0100" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\mathcal{B}=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343293} {:answer/id #uuid "cfa30883-6751-55c6-b0ee-fe2f697d5ba9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\mathcal{B}=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344063} {:answer/id #uuid "d766a2df-5fbb-553e-b26c-26f93187db41" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\mathcal{B}=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344131} {:answer/id #uuid "efb373b6-5224-59a4-a7a4-bdc6d2e7a6af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type