lumns, while the $2$nd column is a non-pivot column.\n\nRemember that we need to pick the pivot columns from the *original matrix*, not from the reduced one.\n\nThe $1$st and $3$rd columns from the original matrix are ${\\mathbf{a}}_{1}$ and ${\\mathbf{a}}_{3}.$ So, a basis of $S$ is $\\{{\\mathbf{a}}_{1},{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}\\},$ that is to say, \n\n$$\n\\mathcal{B}=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}\\}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345009 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15706f7d-fa4e-5373-8ab0-28f245b1898a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\mathcal{B}=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342428} {:answer/id #uuid "388ffd1b-44a7-5b05-aeb3-9ea87351970c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\mathcal{B}=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342703} {:answer/id #uuid "8dc1b14a-1842-5451-91f0-d0429d1f4f5e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\mathcal{B}=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343478} {:answer/id #uuid "a162d6e2-b381-5358-8f39-dcf7857f91d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\mathcal{B}=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}-6 \\\\ -9 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343661} {:answer/id #uuid "d90780cc-a7e2-537c-8faa-7ba7f8342821" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\mathcal{B}=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}-6 \\\\ -9 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344143}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "388ffd1b-44a7-5b05-aeb3-9ea87351970c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\mathcal{B}=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342703} :answer-field/i