he $1$st and $2$nd columns are pivot columns, while the $3$rd column is a non-pivot column.\n\nRemember that we need to pick the pivot columns from the *original matrix*, not from the reduced one.\n\nThe $1$st and $2$nd columns from the original matrix are ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}.$ So, a basis of $S$ is $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\},$ that is to say, \n\n$$\nB=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}10 \\\\ 16\\end{bmatrix}\\}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489274 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28f8bb97-2bc4-5dc8-af62-80dc0012c72c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}15 \\\\ 10 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488556} {:answer/id #uuid "769b2e11-b333-500c-84a5-51aa4d8c16b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488705} {:answer/id #uuid "991e9362-9655-5cf0-a0be-aaa13d573c9f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488777} {:answer/id #uuid "d19e6191-26d5-53a3-95c7-65dc2640adef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}15 \\\\ 10 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488899} {:answer/id #uuid "d81d6455-dfab-5856-82d0-2c4f85caa5c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488917}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d81d6455-dfab-5856-82d0-2c4f85caa5c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488917} :answer-field/id #uuid "de1a4479-26db-5da3-9251-