bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\\right\\}.\n$$\n\nThese pivot columns are linearly independent and span the column space of $A$, which is $S$. The nonpivot columns can be removed without changing the span. Row operations locate the pivot indices; use the original vectors when writing the basis."}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Basis of the Space Spanned by a Set of Vectors by Identifying Pivot Columns"}]}
